CORE no-new-smt
main.c
--isolate-properties --trace --paths lifo
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ not one: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ not two: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ holds: SUCCESS$
^  x=1 \(0+ 0+ 0+ 0+1\)$
^  x=2 \(0+ 0+ 0+ 0+10\)$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Each property is decided in a solver call of its own, and the trace for each
failing property comes from the model of that call.
